# What a source archive of the repository leaves out: GitHub's tarballs and `git archive` honour
# export-ignore, a clone does not. Claudio's workspaces and Shipcast's launches download the tarball
# at a tag (docs/workspaces.md), and these three made it 81 MB of the 100 MB cap for what reading or
# building the source never needs.
#
# The design system's reference screenshots: the agents that compare a screen with them work in a
# checkout (docs/design-system.md).
docs/design-system/reference/screenshots export-ignore
# The README's media: GitHub shows them from the repository; Shipcast's launch.yml demo is read from
# its own clone, not from the archive.
docs/media export-ignore
# The CLI recordings the code-host and tracker tests replay. Without them the tests of
# packages/core do not run from an archive; they run from a checkout, as CI does.
packages/core/test/fixtures/recordings export-ignore
